            <ArticleTitle>Non-puerperal uterine inversion in a patient with intracranial sigmoid sinus thrombosis and facial palsy.</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1136/bcr-2014-206937</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">bcr2014206937</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Non-puerperal uterine inversion and cranial nerve palsies in patients with sigmoid sinus thrombosis are both extremely rare. We report a case of a patient who presented with both simultaneously. The symptoms of sigmoid sinus thrombosis resolved with subcutaneous enoxaparin, and an abdominal dissection with removal of the uterus vaginally resulted in a successful outcome for the patient.</AbstractText>
                <CopyrightInformation>2015 BMJ Publishing Group Ltd.</CopyrightInformation>
            </Abstract>
